The plane $\kappa^\perp$ varies with the label. To compare the equation on the envelope with the one at the origin and to differentiate it in the labels, we express $V$ in coordinates in a fixed $\mathbb R^2$. Choose a constant $3\times2$ matrix with orthonormal columns spanning $k_*^\perp$, let $A_\perp$ be $D_aX$ times this matrix, and let $A_\perp^\dagger=(A_\perp^TA_\perp)^{-1}A_\perp^T$. The columns of $A_\perp$ span $\kappa^\perp$, since $\kappa=(D_aX)^{-T}k_*$, and $A_\perp^\dagger$ takes a vector to its coordinates in those columns after orthogonal projection onto their span. Thus $A_\perp^\dagger A_\perp=\operatorname{Id}_{\mathbb R^2}$ and $A_\perp A_\perp^\dagger=\operatorname{Id}-P_\kappa$. Here $v$ in $V=A_\perp v$ denotes the two coordinates of the transverse velocity. Since $\partial_tA_\perp=MA_\perp$, the equation (5.17) becomes $$\begin{equation}
 v_t+\mathcal M_\perp v=\psi,\qquad
 \mathcal M_\perp=2A_\perp^\dagger MA_\perp,\qquad
 \psi=A_\perp^\dagger f. \tag{5.18}
\end{equation}$$

