*Proof of Theorem 1.1.* Fix a compact $K\subset\mathbb T^3\setminus\{0\}$ and integers $m,q\ge0$. The support balls of the oscillations shrink to the origin, so $O_j$ vanishes on a neighborhood of $[0,T_\infty]\times K$ for all large $j$. Choose $n$ beyond this index and the finitely many thresholds $j_{m,i}$ for $0\le i\le q$. Summing (1.2) on the common interval gives $$\sum_{i=0}^q
 \|\partial_t^i(U_\ell-U_n)\|_{C([0,T_\infty];C^m(K))}
 \le(q+1)\sum_{j=n+1}^{\ell}\lambda_j^{-1}
 \qquad(\ell>n).$$ The right side tends to zero uniformly in $\ell>n$. The finitely many earlier approximants are smooth across $T_\infty$ because $S_j>T_\infty$. The limit agrees with $u$ before $T_\infty$ by Proposition M.8.1.
